      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological-insulator concept established a major new framework for quantum materials, with broad influence on condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele developed the theoretical prediction; Molenkamp's experiments provided a key demonstration. This balances theory and decisive material realization.",
        "maturity": "The underlying topological phases and their experimental signatures have been studied across many systems for years.",
        "uncertainties": [
