        "Shinji Yuasa",
        "Stuart S. P. Parkin",
        "William H. Butler"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Large tunnel magnetoresistance in MgO junctions enabled a major advance in spintronics and practical magnetic data storage, grounded in a clear physical effect.",
        "attribution": "Butler's theory and the experimental demonstrations by Yuasa and Parkin are complementary and central to the crystalline-MgO result.",
        "maturity": "The effect has been independently reproduced and incorporated into technologies, giving it strong confirmation and practical consequence.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broader history of tunnel magnetoresistance includes important earlier work, so the award's scope should stay focused on the MgO-junction breakthrough."
        ]
      }
    },
